Research done (read-only, nothing in the repo changed). Recommendation: run ClaudeHistory and ClaudeSessions forked (hub.fork). In-process, the loop stalls for the whole call: on this machine's 1.92 GB history a cold list_sessions takes 16 s CPU and each search 20 s CPU (37-83 s wall under load), and in-process calls over 30 s were dropped by Mojo's inactivity_timeout. Forked, the hub stall stays under 110 ms and the hub RSS at 67 MB. Biggest secondary finding: the Docker image and the PAR binary decode with pure-Perl Mojo::JSON (about 70x slower). Seven proposed cards and the full numbers are in the previous note; scripts and results are in the scratch dir w-k40/results.md.

